# Test: ze doctor self-heals a corrupt/unreadable blob store instead of wedging.
#
# VALIDATES: storage.NewBlob moves an unreadable database.zefs aside to
#   <path>.replaced-<date> and recreates a valid store, so ze doctor comes up
#   ready (exit 0) instead of failing on a doctor-store-integrity error every
#   run. Covers the incident where a 0-byte database.zefs (left by an
#   interrupted or concurrent write) wedged storage.
# PREVENTS: regression of the zefs "mmap: empty file" wedge, where NewBlob chose
#   Open vs Create by file existence (os.Stat) rather than validity, so any
#   unreadable store broke startup permanently until manual removal.

option=env:var=ZE_CONFIG_DIR:value=.

# Seed an unreadable (non-zefs) database.zefs in the config dir. zefs.Open fails
# on it exactly as it does on the 0-byte file from the original incident, so it
# drives the same self-heal path deterministically.
tmpfs=database.zefs:terminator=EOF_DB
not a valid zefs store
EOF_DB

tmpfs=probe.conf:terminator=EOF_CONF
# ze config
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze doctor --json probe.conf
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stderr:contains=moved unreadable blob aside
